James inquired about the word limit for a fellowship proposal, specifically whether the 2000-word count includes references. I clarified that while it is common for such limits to refer only to the main text, guidelines can vary by organization. I advised James to reach out to the fellowship administrators for confirmation, suggesting that he aim to keep the proposal's core content within the limit while leaving room for references. I recommended using in-text citations to save space and emphasized the importance of including a well-crafted reference list to showcase his engagement with existing research.
